artner’s attributes"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"To build closeness, have two people take turns answering a series of progressively deeper questions — no script needed"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"Long-distance relationships aren’t worse than local ones — the real challenge comes in the first three months after moving in together"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"Check registration statistics before listening to elders: what do “marriage rate” and “divorce rate” actually mean?"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"Accounting for the health benefits of marriage while adjusting for observational data"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Discussing labor division before marriage helps clarify unpaid work responsibilities"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"First check the default legal rules regarding marriage money and property, then decide whether to make a written agreement"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-11"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"When parents pay for a house, they should clearly state whether it’s a loan or a gift at the time of transfer"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"Money borrowed by a spouse in a large amount — if you didn’t sign or later acknowledge it, it doesn’t automatically become your debt"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-13"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Obtaining a marriage certificate requires only an ID card and a signed declaration — no household register needed, no fees, and issuance is immediate"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-14"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["14"]},"Undergoing a premarital medical exam: if a serious illness is present, it must be disclosed before marriage registration"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-15"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["15"]},"Calculating the cost of walking away: Divorce by mutual agreement requires a 30-day cooling-off period, while divorce via litigation has strict legal prerequisites"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-16"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["16"]},"Make a separate tally for the benefits to your elders when they get married — don’t mix it with your own records"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-17"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["17"]},"Treating relationship quality as a health factor: focus on the issue, not the person — avoid insults and sarcasm"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-18"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["18"]},"While both partners are of sound mind, complete power of attorney, designated guardianship, and wills: Legally, you are not close relatives; without these, you will have no signing authority or inheritance rights."]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/10-19","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["19"]},"Don’t marry while hiding your sexual orientation, and don’t treat “marriage of convenience” as an easy shortcut: legally, it is a real marriage, and the only way out is divorce"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/10-20"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["20"]},"When a relationship is stuck in endless arguments and silent treatment, couples therapy can help — waiting alone rarely does"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/10"},"children":["Chapter 10"," ·"," ","Is it worth dating and getting married?"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"10-19"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["19"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-a"},"children":["Evidence"," ","A"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["Don’t marry while hiding your sexual orientation, and don’t treat “marriage of convenience” as an easy shortcut: legally, it is a real marriage, and the only way out is divorce"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["Marrying while concealing one’s sexual orientation is not legally invalid, nor can it be annulled; the only way to end it is through divorce. A “marriage of convenience” is also a real marriage, so any income earned or debts incurred afterward are treated as joint marital property. When the deceived spouse files for divorce, they may request a larger share of assets and compensation for emotional distress, though whether the court will grant this remains uncertain."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["There is no financial cost. The hard part is resisting fam…"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Article 1051 of the Civil Code lists only three grounds on which a marriage can be declared invalid: bigamy, p…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: Don’t marry while hiding your sexual orientation, and don’t treat “marriage of convenience” as an easy shortcut: legally, it is a real marriage, and the only way out is divorce"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["There is no financial cost. The hard part is resisting family pressure to stay married — this may go on for many years."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Article 1051 of the Civil Code lists only three grounds on which a marriage can be declared invalid: bigamy, prohibited familial relationships, and underage marriage. Articles 1052 and 1053 allow annulment only in cases of coercion or concealed serious illnesses prior to marriage. Interpretation (I) of the Marriage and Family Section, Article 17, states that any other grounds for invalidation will be rejected by courts. Hence, divorce is the sole legal exit route. A registered “marriage of convenience” is likewise lawful. Article 1062 designates post‑marriage wages, bonuses, and other earnings as joint property, while Article 1064 treats debts jointly signed or incurred for household needs as joint obligations. Divorce damages are covered in Article 1091, limited to bigamy, cohabitation with a third party, domestic violence, abuse, abandonment, or “other major faults”; Interpretation (I), Article 2 restricts “cohabitation with a third party” to opposite‑sex relationships. Thus, same‑sex relationships must rely on the “other major faults” clause for compensation claims, which may include emotional distress awards — these must be requested at the time of filing for divorce, otherwise they won’t be granted. No court rulings on such cases have been published since the Civil Code took effect; however, a 2013 article on the Jiangsu Provincial Higher People’s Court website discussed a wife suing for divorce after discovering her husband’s homosexuality, presenting two viewpoints: one argued that homosexuality did not qualify as a statutory fault, so no extra assets or compensation should be awarded; the author supported the opposite stance, advocating that the deceived spouse be treated as “innocent” and thus entitled to asset protection and emotional damages nationwide."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Original sources"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":["全国人大 (2020). 民法典（第一千零五十一至一千零五十四、一千零六十二、一千零六十四、一千零七十九、一千零八十七、一千零九十一条）. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://flk.npc.gov.cn/detail?id=ff808081729d1efe01729d50b5c500bf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://flk.npc.gov.cn/detail?id=ff808081729d1efe01729d50b5c500bf"]},"（国家法律法规数据库）；最高人民法院 (2020). 关于适用《中华人民共和国民法典》婚姻家庭编的解释（一）（法释〔2020〕22 号，第二、十七、八十六至九十条）. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://flk.npc.gov.cn/detail?id=ff80808177e75f880178006736f21aaf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://flk.npc.gov.cn/detail?id=ff80808177e75f880178006736f21aaf"]},"；朱来宽、王洪娟 (2013). 因同性恋导致离婚能否主张损害赔偿？江苏法院网. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"http://www.jsfy.gov.cn/article/26621.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["http://www.jsfy.gov.cn/article/26621.html"]}]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://flk.npc.gov.cn/detail?id=ff808081729d1efe01729d50b5c500bf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"life-source-link"},"children":["Open source link"," ",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"13","height":"13","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M15 3h6v6"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M10 14 21 3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Book note"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-content-reference"},"children":["Only one analytical article mentions the possibility of extra assets and emotional compensation; it does not describe any actual verdict, so success depends on the specific court. The Civil Code introduced “other major faults” as a new legal basis, giving the deceived spouse a stronger argument. The statutory provisions themselves merit an A rating. If both parties in a “marriage of convenience” each have same‑sex partners, those partners receive no marital protections, and any related property arrangements must be specified separately — see Section 18 on same‑sex guardianship and wills. Divorce procedures, including the 30‑day cooling‑off period or litigation, follow the same rules as any other divorce; see Section 15. Waiving compensation claims in a divorce agreement bars any later legal pursuit. The primary beneficiaries are the deceived spouse; the other party also faces consequences such as divorce, asset division, and child‑custody disputes once the deception is uncovered."]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-personal-note"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["My note"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button"},"children":["Write a reminder for yourself…"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager-link","href":"/en/tip/10-18"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-left","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M19 12H5"},"children":[]}]},{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"small","props":{},"children":["Previous"]},"While both partners are of sound mind, complete power of attorney, designated guardianship, and wills: Legally, you are not close relatives; without these, you will have no signing authority or inheritance rights."]}]},{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager-link next","href":"/en/tip/10-20"},"children":[{"tag":"span","p